{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/58554-mormon-hunter-groups","id":58554,"title":"Mormon hunter groups?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-26T23:44:45-08:00","id":58554,"title":"Mormon hunter groups?","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I am working on a hunter game and one religion I am looking at using are the mormons. However, I do not know much about Mormonism. I did discover that there was a group by the name of the Danites who did exist as a vigiliante group to protect them during the early years. <br /> <br /> Though, I am not sure which supernatural, would be their main foe. Also not sure on what sort of Endownments that they would get would be like. <br /> <br /> So if anyone has any advice on using Mormon hunters or just want to help me out here, feel free <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -herkles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T00:55:24-08:00","id":58569,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind the Danites are a touchy subject as they feature prominently in anti-Mormon propaganda historically - Joseph Smith himself ended up disavowing them entirely in the harshest terms theologically possible.<br /> <br /> Of course, one could say the same thing of the actual book Malleus Maleficarum, so just be aware of it while you do it. MM works because they're NOT supposed to be an accurate representation of the Catholic Church, its teachings, or answerable to proper Church authority - they're a heretical conspiracy. If you're going to draw on the darker aspects of the Danites, you should probably emphasize the history of hostility between them and the actual Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T03:11:46-08:00","id":58604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/58554-mormon-hunter-groups?p=58569#post58569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you're going to draw on the darker aspects of the Danites, you should probably emphasize the history of hostility between them and the actual Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mormonism has a <a href=\"http://\u200bhttp://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_sects_in_the_Latter_Day_Saint_movement\" target=\"_blank\">history of breakaway sects</a>, so it would be no problem too represent the Mormon Hunters as belonging too a heretical and small sect or cult.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1072-theye1","name":"theye1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1072_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T05:30:51-08:00","id":58641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/58554-mormon-hunter-groups?p=58569#post58569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind the Danites are a touchy subject as they feature prominently in anti-Mormon propaganda historically - Joseph Smith himself ended up disavowing them entirely in the harshest terms theologically possible.<br /> <br /> Of course, one could say the same thing of the actual book Malleus Maleficarum, so just be aware of it while you do it. MM works because they're NOT supposed to be an accurate representation of the Catholic Church, its teachings, or answerable to proper Church authority - they're a heretical conspiracy. If you're going to draw on the darker aspects of the Danites, you should probably emphasize the history of hostility between them and the actual Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be an interesting twist - the Danites still exist as a secret society within the LDS, but believe that the church has been infiltrated by some supernatural force (Demons, perhaps), so they're kind of Mormon double-agents, protecting their church from threats both without and within.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T07:46:18-08:00","id":58707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/58554-mormon-hunter-groups?p=58641#post58641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could be an interesting twist - the Danites still exist as a secret society within the LDS, but believe that the church has been infiltrated by some supernatural force (Demons, perhaps), so they're kind of Mormon double-agents, protecting their church from threats both without and within.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is kind of what I was going for, a secret society for the LDS church that is their answer to fighting back against the monsters. The fact that their is some propaganda against them, makes it more interesting to me. <br /> <br /> Anyways, which monster would they fight primarly? I want to avoid using vampires, yet again. Also what kind of Endowment makes sense for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T13:31:26-08:00","id":59075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyways, which monster would they fight primarly? </div> </div> </div>With a history of sects breaking off, maybe they go after witches or even Mummies; the two groups that seem most devoted to creating cults. If you want to go weirder, you could bring in the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also what kind of Endowment makes sense for them? </div> </div> </div>None. Unless there's a compelling back story, I think it'd be kinda odd giving them some special ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:29:22-08:00","id":59141,"title":"","content":"Poke ArcaneWatcher onto to this thread. Arc had ideas for this before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:49:17-08:00","id":59164,"title":"","content":"I have my own particular vision of Mormon compacts and conspiracies based on the folklore and the church's take on history as well as the insider's perspective on the issues of the church-my compacts tie into the perversion of the doctrine that Mormon culture regularly delves into dressed up in folklore of the Church since it's inception,and my conspiracies tie back into the Book of Mormon history around one of the more interesting conspiracy ideas that emerges from it and centers on the idea of 'acceptable compromise'. What I'm saying is that my own projects might lead to some place different than Herkles, if for no other reason than he's looking at it from the outside.<br /> <br /> That said, yes, I am available for subverting, deconstructing and challenging my faith in the pursuit of the Vigil.<br /> <br /> Allow me to back up and ask a few questions to help you work out your own vision. As far as the Mormon church goes, what is it about the LDS faith/culture/history that you feels leads to a good narrative struggle or examination of the Vigil through that lens? In short, why do you want to use Mormons as a base for a compact or conspiracy? Or another way, what is the theme of this group?<br /> <br /> This will help me determine which facets of church history/folklore/doctrine/etc. would be the most evocative for your idea, as well as helping me marry it to an aspect of the World of Darkness. There's a little bit of something, whether it be openly practiced today or shed off some time ago, that ties into just about every supernatural(Hell, sooner or later I intend to write this whole paper on how Mage metaphysics and Mormon faith relate to one another), so I need something to hone in on.<br /> <br /> I will also read up again on the Danites, since you expressed an interest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T19:39:02-08:00","id":59398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/58554-mormon-hunter-groups?p=59164#post59164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow me to back up and ask a few questions to help you work out your own vision. As far as the Mormon church goes, what is it about the LDS faith/culture/history that you feels leads to a good narrative struggle or examination of the Vigil through that lens? In short, why do you want to use Mormons as a base for a compact or conspiracy? Or another way, what is the theme of this group?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few things. I am setting my game within the Dallas-Fort Worth metroplex, and wiki says that there is a sizable LDS church community. So the fact that it is there is one reason I want to use them. I also like learning about other beliefs, and I will openly admit that I am not that familiar at all with Mormonism. I know it was born within America, and that they moved out west in the 1800s but really that is about it. <br /> <br /> There are two main things in particular that make me interested.<br /> <br /> 1.) It is an organized church that is not the Catholic Church. While I certinly shall use the catholics, I like having another choice, and their already is a sizable LDS church community in DFW. However, I am not very familar in how different is in structure compared to the Catholic Church which I am far more familar with.<br /> <br /> 2.) The whole Missionary Services. This is not only rife for plot hooks but also gives hunters a convenient reason to not only have backup but also to knock on the monster's door. This is one thing that I wish to use with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:44:06-08:00","id":59568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/58554-mormon-hunter-groups?p=59398#post59398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are a few things. I am setting my game within the Dallas-Fort Worth metroplex, and wiki says that there is a sizable LDS church community. So the fact that it is there is one reason I want to use them. I also like learning about other beliefs, and I will openly admit that I am not that familiar at all with Mormonism. I know it was born within America, and that they moved out west in the 1800s but really that is about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, some basics (these are gross simplifications, and I'm speaking as an outsider who has studied the subject from a secular pov, I in no way mean to elevate secular-academic pov on a religion over insider-theological pov, both have value), focusing on areas of difference from other forms of Christianity (so only a sliver of the totality of the faith, but I'm not bothering to explain things like Original Sin, salvation through Christ's sacrifice, etc etc)<br /> <br /> - Mormonism is a distinctly American faith in many regards (not that there isn't a quickly growing non-American Mormon population, there is! I just mean it's nature reflects its core American elements). The history presented in the Book of Mormon is that of Pre-Columbian Americas as a land settled by Lost Tribes of Israel - many of whom (primarily the Nephites) accepted Christ when he appeared to them after the resurrection and delivered a further testament. These are who wrote and buried the Golden Plates that were revealed to Joseph Smith in the 19th Century. These Christians of the Americas died off before European settlers arrived, and only the descendants of those who spiritually lost their way remained.<br /> <br /> - This theology ties into 19th Century Manifest Destiny in many ways, as it presents the Americas as a historically Christian and white (the Israelites were originally white according to the Book of Mormon, with darker skin amongst native peoples being mark of having being cut off from God - please note the modern Church has worked hard to shed this racial baggage, and modern Mormons do not interpret these references to skin-tone literally), and the west becomes the new Promised Land (starting from New York, initially &quot;the West&quot; was Missouri - where the original Garden of Eden was to have existend; but then they had to push further Westward to survive due to persecution).<br /> <br /> - Interesting theological note: there is no distinction between a human soul and an Angelic being in Mormonism. All spirits have a pre-mortal and post-mortal existence. So while dead people becoming angels is a common misconception for most Abrahamic faiths, it's accurate in Mormonism. Adam was the Archangel Michael. Jesus was Jehovah (not to be confused with his Father, Elohim: more commonly simply 'Heavenly Father')...<br /> <br /> - There are three distinct beings within the Godhead, unlike the united Trinity shared by Catholics, Orthodox Christians, and most (not all!) Protestants. Jesus walked this world just as his Father did before him in some other iteration of the universe. The Heavenly Father is a being of flesh and bone.<br /> <br /> - Like Catholicism, and unlike predominant strands of Protestant theology (Luther's Justification by Faith Alone, and Calvin's external salvation through Grace alone), free will and ritual actions play central roles in salvation in Mormon theology. First off - free will is the root of the original fall - Lucifer didn't want it to exist, Jehovah (who is pre-mortal Jesus) did, as free will means the choice to be righteous and good would give glory to God.<br /> <br /> At the end of days, the only people cast into the &quot;Outer Darkness&quot; will be the ones who choose it. Post-mortal existence means the opportunity to accept salvation don't stop in life. So the &quot;Sons of Perdition&quot; who follow Lucifer do so knowingly by choice, because that must be the case for free will to have meaning.<br /> <br /> However, while salvation can be accepted after death, there are levels of Exaltation - and the HIGHEST level of Exaltation is reserved for those who were baptized into the Church (note that this is why the Church does posthumous baptisms for the ancestors of Mormon converts), and who are sealed in &quot;celestial marriage&quot;. Family is central and deeply theological in Mormonism.<br /> <br /> This highest level of Exaltation entails becoming as unto God, continuing the cycle of universes. Yes, with the previous prerequisite, this does imply there is a Heavenly Mother (no, she's not the Holy Spirit [repository of the divine feminine in medieval theology], or the Virgin Mary). The Mormons I've discussed this with say she's respected but not talked about a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> - As it's one of the things uninformed people are likely to have heard of, I'll briefly address plural marriage. It's a non-issue in the modern LDS Church itself, which abandoned the practice over a century ago (as with shedding the racial baggage, these reforms are possible while remaining theologically coherent because the President of the Church and the Quorum are 'prophets, seers, and revealators' subject to direct divine guidance). It is of historic note however, because both of the major schisms in the Church were rooted in it. Firstly, after Joseph Smith was martyred in Missouri, those who followed Brigham Young to what would become Utah adhered to plural marriage, on the basis of returning to the traditions of the Ancient Israelites. Those who remained in Missouri following Joseph Smith III rejected the practice (many biographers believe that Joseph Smith Jr[the original prophet]'s original wife, Emma Hale Smith, Joseph Smith III's mother, was less than pleased when her husband adopted the practice late in his ministry, and her son sympathized with her). While the former became the well known Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints, the latter became the Reorganized Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints (today known as the Community of Christ) - often seen as the &quot;mainstream Protestantism friendly&quot; offshoot of the Latter Day Saints movement.<br /> <br /> On the other extreme, you have the Fundamentalist Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints - which split off in the early 20th Century when the LDS Church moved to excommunicate those Mormons who fought to continue plural marriage. It exists in isolated enclaves in the Southwest and continues the practice today. It also adheres to the old racial philosophy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, that's all that's springing to mind as &quot;basic differences between Mormonism and other forms of Christianity&quot; - and is obviously grossly simplified and basic. ArcaneArts can give you a much more human outlook on the lived experience of the Church itself (as well as a lot of insightful folklore and biblical history details of real improtance to the faithful) than my academic wall-splatter.<br /> <br /> Just to clear up anyone's doubts: YES Mormonism is a Christian tradition; it centers on salvation via Christ's death and resurrection.<br /> <br /> The reason people often want to paint it as not Christian (beyond the normal bigotries that result in [for example] some hardline Catholics and Protestants claiming the other isn't Christian) is because of the erroneous reductionism that makes people want to force all Christian traditions into either the &quot;Catholic&quot; or &quot;Protestant&quot; box (I've seriously seen people argue that Orthodox Christians are Protestants on this basis, it's ridiculous). Mormonism is NOT a Protestant tradition, and beyond the principles shared by all Christians, has nothing in common with those movements. It is a completely distinct form of Christianity like Catholicism, Orthodox Christianity, and Protestantism (or &quot;lost&quot; traditions like Gnosticism or Arianism).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-28-2014, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T00:10:03-08:00","id":59579,"title":"","content":"Fun Fact: Thanks to the Church's post-mortuum baptism efforts for the ancestors of all who join the Church, Salt Lake City has the most massive genealogy database in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T01:05:20-08:00","id":59607,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there are any Lucifuge members hanging out around there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T06:06:13-08:00","id":59735,"title":"","content":"Glamour's thing is going to be fun to read through when I get back. Wonder if I'll have to proof-check it.EDIT: Eh, like,a few details no one will stress over, but academically that's a good summation.<br /> <br /> In the mean time, are there are any Lucifuge members hanging out there? Oh, without a a doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-28-2014, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T07:25:35-08:00","id":59781,"title":"","content":"I was going off memory, so I'm not surprised I missed some details. I'm just glad I didn't fuck anything up enough to offend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T09:37:33-08:00","id":59897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/58554-mormon-hunter-groups?p=59568#post59568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> snip</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks for the info. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T13:30:08-08:00","id":60088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/58554-mormon-hunter-groups?p=59568#post59568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, while salvation can be accepted after death, there are levels of Exaltation - and the HIGHEST level of Exaltation is reserved for those who were baptized into the Church (note that this is why the Church does posthumous baptisms for the ancestors of Mormon converts), and who are sealed in &quot;celestial marriage&quot;. Family is central and deeply theological in Mormonism.</div> </div> </div> </div>This suggests that Sin-Eaters will be a common foe for the Mormons. Some Sin-Eaters will be want to protect the Ghosts from their descendants. Others will think the baptism is fine but object to ignorant mortals doing anything to the dead on principle. The third group will think it's a great idea, claim it was theirs all along, and then compete with Mormons on the posthumous baptism buisness.<br /> <br /> Plus Sin-Eaters probably have the most cults of any major splat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T13:56:07-08:00","id":60104,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty interesting idea, though what would you see the Sin-Eaters antagonists actually doing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T14:13:05-08:00","id":60118,"title":"","content":"Assuming that mass murder isn't the Sin-Eaters style - you could argue it either way, but I prefer to say not - I could see them building magic foci in Haunts to block the mormon's power from reaching the Underworld; stuff for the hunters to smash basically.<br /> <br /> Ocasionally I could see them abducting and killing or dong some kind of weird exorcism on someone who got their ancestors baptised when they want to help a specific ghost.<br /> <br /> They might act like invisible tempting demons. Floating around twilight pushing thoughts of vice into &quot;pure mormons&quot; heads.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't really like the idea of Sin-Eaters being walking murder machines, it doesn't fit Geist's themes that well. So I'd portray them sort of like a very annoying yet only moderately dangerous (read as: without hunters there would be mass slaughter, with vigilant hunters only a few deaths) pest who you can't get rid off.<br /> <br /> They're constantly building these weird things that make everyone uncomfortable and block Mormon rituals or tempting people to betray Mormon virtues in general or to join their Krewe/Cults in specific however since the Hunters have them outnumbered they rarely provoke physical fights.<br /> <br /> During daylight the Hunters and Bound just glare at each other and try not to do anything that will get the police involved - Sin-Eaters don't want their back accounts frozen. When no one's looking the hunters smash wards and try to drive off projecting Sin-Eaters. Physical fights are rare because the Bound are outnumbered, out resourced, and good at vanishing but even when the Hunters kill one it rarely sticks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-28-2014, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T21:43:38-08:00","id":60444,"title":"","content":"I wanna knock this out of the way-I'm actually not crazy about monster focused compacts and conspiracies, or at least singularly focused ones. Cheiron, Task Force Valkyrie, Ascending Ones-a lot of the best ones come from the Core, and the focus is less on &quot;THis monster is wrong&quot; and more &quot;This is our goal, our philosophy&quot;. Even AKD and the Lucifuge have some broad focuses that make them far more interesting than the more focused organizations. So for the purposes of this discussion, I'm not going that angle. That's not to imply that there isn't something to angle of Sin Eaters though, but I'll get back to that.<br /> <br /> I got distracted today, anddidn't even get to homework, so I can't go over the internal church look, so today'll be response.<br /> <br /> First, details that Glamour got wrong.<br /> <br /> 1)THe entire skin thing is now a huge muddled mess, further compounded that on the one hand the early church did think that God did curse the Lamanites with darker skin(not African black, which is one thing that does get lost in the shuffle), and yet at the same time the early church had no problem giving the priesthood to blacks and other ethnicities. I don't intend to dwell on this as it is such a mess of truth and fiction to untangle, just a minor note.<br /> <br /> 2)That place in Missouri is not Eden, it's where the Saints will gather before the coming of Christ. Again, not a big deal.<br /> <br /> 3)Not that it's a doctrinal thing, I just find it funny to think about how Descent plays out in regards to the &quot;people are angels&quot; thing- ironically, that makes demons almost a direct corollary to Mormon belief. If it weren't for the fact the church is squeamish about the imagery as a culture(ridiculously so), I'd almost claim that as grounds for being friends.<br /> <br /> 4)THe ritual action behind the sacrament, baptisms, enacting of the priesthood, temple covenants, etc. is one of the big reasons why the church is often viewed as a cult. THe Ritual action is completely true, I'm just say that from a dramatic point building on that is a fun narrative image.<br /> <br /> 5) It takes more than just willingly choosing Perdition to end up in Outer Darkness-it's not like claiming to be a Satanist will get you screwed over. In order to do so requires a perfect knowledge of the truth of the Gospel and the rejection thereof. Pre-mortal existence, this was somewhat easier,although a lot dafter-but that's why the a third could fall. THe number of people who have gone to Outer Darkness since the Fall is hard to count(although it can be counted on one hand! 5, 10, 15.....) and really not important-most people don't get that kind of knowledge due to the accountability they would have to it.<br /> <br /> You know, I'm actually really enjoying a Demon the Descent angle on the church, which brings me around to.....<br /> <br /> Second, the Sin Eater angle.<br /> <br /> Firstly, I actually kind of enjoy the idea of Joseph Smith dying in the First Vision and having Moroni actually be a geist, with the church emerging from his channel down the line. Alternatively,I'm also amused by the idea of Joseph Smith having made a demonic pact and trading out with a Demon, the church being from there possibly the largest Integrator scheme ever conceived. But that's neither here nor there. EDIT: Or maybe it's a weird synergy between the two of them?<br /> <br /> It merits mention that actually Mormons are more likely to be conflicted but possibly enthralled by Sin Eaters. Sin Eaters deal with ghosts, angels, and demons and mythologies in general that lends an odd credence to their ideas. On the other hand, the supernatural junk culture of Sin Eaters involves a lot of paganistic and pop cultural approaches to things, which again makes the general masses squirm. The relationship would be odd, sometimes strained, sometimes really close. Which, frankly, feels right-that's how Mormons as a culture are with most of the world. If the emphasis is on the missionary aspect of the church-well, let me just say that there's a reason that the Church's extensive missionary efforts is one of my favorite things to play around with as a base for compacts. It's a Book of Mormon in one hand and a gun in the other and the missionaries never really know which to hold tighter.<br /> <br /> On a different front, because I love exploitation for 'good reasons', part of me is enthralled with the idea of a Mormon Conspiracy that draws on a warped 'priesthood' to use Sin-Eaters as a more direct method of post-mortem salvation, but I have very little idea of where to begin with.<br /> <br /> A lot of this depends on the themes that Herkles wants to play with, which is motive to try and chat about the doctrine tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T06:59:43-08:00","id":60721,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification on Missouri (though I do have some Mormon sources that claim it's where Eden was, so it may be an issue of doctrinal shift or dispute), and for the info about the early Church allowing a multi-racial priesthood, I hadn't realized that! Idid know Smith was an abolitionist and the inhabitants of the Utah territory remained firmly Union-aligned during the Civil War, so I'm not surprised that it's an issue the early Church was better on than during the middle period, when the whole country was surging into defacto segregationism in the spirit of North/South [white] reunification.<br /> <br /> The other points I think we're copacetic on, I just didn't do a good enough job explaining late at night (I should have been clearer about what choosing the Outer Darkness meant for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-29-2014, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"}